'''''Dichondra micrantha''''', the '''Asian ponysfoot'''<ref name="United States Fish and Wildlife Service - Asian Ponysfoot - overview">{{cite web |title=Asian Ponysfoot - overview |url=https://www.fws.gov/species/asian-ponysfoot-dichondra-micrantha |website=[[United States Fish and Wildlife Service]] |access-date=26 May 2024}}</ref> or '''lawnleaf''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Convolvulaceae]].<ref name="PfaF_Dm" >{{cite web |url=https://pfaf.org/user/Plant.aspx?LatinName=Dichondra+micrantha |title=''Dichondra micrantha'' - Urb. |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=13 June 2023 |website=PFAF Plant Database |publisher=Plants for a Future |access-date=26 May 2024 }}</ref><ref name="DIOMI" >{{cite web |url=https://gd.eppo.int/taxon/DIOMI |title=''Dichondra micrantha'' (DIOMI) |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=2024 |website=EPPO Global Database |publisher=European and Mediterranean Plant Protection Organization |access-date=26 May 2024 |quote=Asian pony's foot, lawnleaf }}</ref> It is native to Texas, Mexico, and the Caribbean, and it has been introduced worldwide.<ref name="POWO_79457-2" >{{cite POWO |id=79457-2 |title=''Dichondra micrantha'' Urb. |access-date=26 May 2024 }}</ref> A prostrate perennial reaching {{cvt|4|in|cm|0|order=flip}}, it prefers wetter soils.<ref name="PfaF_Dm" /> In the past it was recommended as a grass substitute in lawns due to its easy maintenance requirements, but proved vulnerable to [[flea beetle]]s.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://hort.extension.wisc.edu/articles/silver-falls-dichondra |title='Silver Falls' ''Dichondra argentea'' |last1=Mahr |first1=Susan |date=2024 |website=Wisconsin Horticulture Division of Extension |publisher=The Board of Regents of the University of Wisconsin System |access-date=26 May 2024 }}</ref>

